*20
/SERINDEX
/FOR PDP-12
/PETER GUTTERMAN
/UNIV. WISCONSIN
/
/SEARCHES FOR A NAME IN A DIAL INDEX
/ ENTER WITH THE NAME TO BE SEARCHED IN
/   MEMORY STARTING AT LOCATION FWA,
/ WITH THE INDEX IN QUARTERS 6 & 7,
/ AND WITH FWA IN THE ACCUMULATOR.
/IF FOUND, INDEX 1 POINTS TO LAST WORD
/ OF THE NAME IN THE INDEX UPON RETURN
/CALLING SEQUENCE:
/  LOAD FWA
/  JMP SINDEX
/  RETURN: NOT FOUND
/  RETURN: FOUND
/NON-INTERRUPTABLE
/
SINDEX,	STC .+15 /SAVE FWA
	ADD 0	 /SAVE RETURN
	STC .+26
	SET I 1 /SET POINTER TO
	7007	/FIRST INDEX ENTRY
	LDA /MOVE INDEX POINTER TO END OF ENTRY
	1
	BSE I
	7
	AZE I	 /END OF INDEX?
	JMP .+16 /YES: SEARCH FAILED
	STC 1	/NO: SAVE INDEX POINTER
	SET I 2
	0	/NAME FWA
	SET I 3 /FOUR WORDS PER NAME
	-4
	LDA 2	/LOAD FIRST 2 CHARACTERS
	JMP .+2 /SKIP
	LDA I 2 /LOAD NEXT 2 CHARACTERS
	SAE I 1 /MATCH TO INDEX?
	JMP .-17 /NO: MOVE TO NEXT ENTRY
	XSK I 3 /ENOUGH MATCHED?
	JMP .-4 /NO: GET NEXT TWO CHARS
	SET I 2 /YES: EXIT TO .+2
	JMP 0 /USE THIS IF SEARCH FAILED
	XSK I 2
	JMP 2	/RETURN IF NAME FOUND
/END SERINDEX
/
